Description: end the whole process with exit_group
 The intro ends with the i386 system call exit (1), which only ends the
 calling thread. The SDL threads (audio callback and, with sdl12-compat,
 SDL 2 event threads) keep running: the main thread becomes a zombie and
 the window stays on the screen, frozen, instead of closing. Use
 exit_group (252) so that the whole process ends.
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-13
--- a/src/inconsistency.asm
+++ b/src/inconsistency.asm
@@ -512,7 +512,7 @@
 
 	exit:
 	call [SDL_CloseAudio]
-	mov eax,1		;EXIT
+	mov eax,252		;exit_group: SDL threads must end too
 	mov ebx,4
 	int 80h
 
